Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from ETSI TS
102 114 V1.6.1 (2019-08), "DTS Coherent Acoustics; Core and Extensions with
Additional Profiles", published free of charge by ETSI. They are not
translations of, and do not derive from, any other DTS implementation's
source. The normative tables (Annex D) were transcribed from the ETSI PDF by
tools/dts_gen_tables.py and cross-checked against the V1.2.1 (2002-12) and,
for D.9 and D.11, V1.4.1 (2012-11) editions.

The two code books no ETSI edition prints (D.10.1, the ADPCM prediction
coefficients, and D.10.2, the high-frequency subband vectors) are not
included and were not taken from anywhere. The crate accepts them from a
caller who holds them; AdpcmCodebook::private_test_book() is a code book of
stable predictors constructed in this crate, not D.10.1.

No other implementation is used in testing, as a library, a program or a
test oracle. The public sample streams the sample tests decode are fetched
at test time, as data, from https://streams.videolan.org/samples/A-codecs/DTS/ and
checked against the SHA-256 sums in tests/samples.rs; they are not
distributed with this crate.

